## Goal
- Primary objective: Build an interactive Mini Crossword puzzle game playable within ServiceNow that automatically generates solvable 5x5 crossword grids from a word dictionary
- Success criteria:
  1. Users can click into any white grid cell and type letters
  2. Keyboard navigation works (arrows, backspace) to move between cells
  3. Real-time validation shows green for correct letters, red for incorrect
  4. Puzzle displays "Congratulations" message upon completion
  5. Clues organized by Across/Down with hints/definitions visible
  6. Puzzle generator creates valid crosswords where all word intersections have matching letters

## Audience
- Users: General ServiceNow users who want to play casual puzzle games
- Skill level: Novice - users should be able to click and type without training
- Usage pattern: Ad-hoc casual gameplay sessions, desktop and mobile devices

## App Identity
- App name: Mini Crossword
- Data classification: Internal
- Theming: Classic crossword puzzle aesthetic - black and white grid, clean borders, traditional newspaper puzzle vibe

## What the App Must Do

### Core Capabilities

1. **Auto-generate valid 5x5 crossword puzzles** from a word dictionary with these constraints:
   - Words can be 2-5 letters long (variable length support)
   - Minimum 3 words required per puzzle
   - First row must contain at least one horizontal word
   - Words must intersect with matching letters at shared cells
   - CRITICAL: ALL horizontal and vertical letter sequences in the grid must form valid dictionary words (no invalid "cross-words")
   - Blank (black) spaces allowed when no valid word fits
   - ALL valid words including those formed by intersections must be identified and recorded
   - Random puzzles use timestamp-based randomization for uniqueness
   - Daily puzzles use date-based seeding for consistency

2. **Display interactive 5x5 crossword grid** with:
   - White squares for letter entry
   - Black squares for blank spaces
   - Yellow highlight on active/selected cell
   - Green background for correct letters
   - Red background for incorrect letters
   - Cell borders creating classic crossword appearance

3. **Accept user input** with full keyboard navigation:
   - Click any white cell to select it
   - Type A-Z letters (automatically converted to uppercase)
   - Backspace deletes current letter and moves to previous cell
   - Arrow keys navigate up/down/left/right through grid
   - Auto-skip over black (blank) cells during navigation
   - Auto-advance to next cell after typing a letter

4. **Validate answers in real-time** by:
   - Comparing each typed letter against the correct answer
   - Immediately showing green (correct) or red (incorrect) feedback
   - Checking puzzle completion when all cells are correct
   - Displaying success message when puzzle is solved

5. **Show organized clues** in two columns:
   - Across clues (left column) - all horizontal words
   - Down clues (right column) - all vertical words
   - Each clue numbered sequentially (1, 2, 3, etc.)
   - Position indicators showing "Row X, Col Y" for starting position
   - Hint/definition text from word dictionary

6. **Auto-load puzzle on page load** - when user opens the page, a random puzzle is automatically selected and displayed

7. **Store word dictionary** with categorization:
   - Words (2-5 letters)
   - Hints (short clues)
   - Definitions (full explanations used as puzzle clues)
   - Categories for themed puzzles (Sports, Food, etc.)

8. **Support both puzzle types**:
   - Daily puzzles: Generated once per day, consistent for that date
   - Random puzzles: Unique each time, timestamp-based randomization

### Reporting Needs
None - this is a casual game application

### SLAs or Service Targets
- Puzzle generation should complete within 10 seconds
- Grid should be responsive and update within 100ms of user input

